# Review audit: USB role workaround and built-in probe timeout

Repository: samcday/pocketboot. Annotated commit:
f52efe969d181c155ba4653753d296adee5b3a8f (normal USB/eMMC startup).
Reviewed again at a7d0397cc3e01e4fe2bb1bb9aa667bc88fcc8006.
Hardware evidence below is from the recorded Lenovo TB-X304F / APQ8017
trials, not a new trial. The review itself was read-only source inspection.
Kernel pin: pem120/linux-msm89x7 a51b91b503307d35902447dd1f90db765372cf3b.

## USB chronology and what the workaround really does

Commands used to establish ordering:

    git show 4f6fa88:patches/kernel/msm8917/0002-arm64-dts-qcom-tbx304x-pocketboot.patch
    git diff 5854328 f52efe9 -- patches/kernel/msm8917/0002-arm64-dts-qcom-tbx304x-pocketboot.patch

The first target commit 4f6fa88 already changed dr_mode from otg to peripheral
and removed both charger extcon and host vbus-supply. The usb-role-switch
property and normal userspace device-role request were added much later in
f52efe9, after controlled diagnostics. It was not an OTG-only failure fixed
by selecting peripheral mode for the first time.

After the RPM and PM_OPP fixes, the first bounded diagnostic logged successful
UDC binding but not-attached / UNKNOWN speed. The next controlled image added
the role-switch interface and requested device role; verified PocketBoot USB
appeared at 5.471 s from the host Linux boot invocation. That trial changed
both the DT interface and the software request; it does not establish a
fundamental need for userspace role selection on this hardware.

Exact-pin source findings:

- core.c:1173-1174 initializes the gadget for dr_mode=peripheral;
  core.c:649-668 already chooses the gadget when that is the only role.
  Static role selection therefore is not the missing part.
- ci_handle_vbus_change in otg.c:131-145 still gates gadget connection on
  B-session-valid for an OTG-capable controller. is_otg is derived from
  hardware capabilities (core.c:975-988), not cleared just because dr_mode
  is peripheral. Without an external source, hw_read_otgsc reads native BSV.
- Adding usb-role-switch changes hw_read_otgsc: otg.c:38-54 replaces BSV
  with the software cable.connected state instead of the hardware value.
- ci_usb_role_switch_set(USB_ROLE_DEVICE), core.c:629-645, sets that
  software VBUS-connected state true and invokes the interrupt handler.
- The MSM reset callback, ci_hdrc_msm.c:117-122, also enables the hardware
  session-valid override when an extcon or role switch exists.

